# The net of effects puts the counts of deeds back behind a call that its row calls quiet, where the call returns. Where it throws they stay as the callee left them, so an edge that holds a turn to having done nothing
# would stop a right program behind the catch. No such edge is built there: a handler is entered with an empty state (`Walker::noteStateAtThrowForHandler()`), so the mark of the turn is down behind the catch.
# The one turn that begins again is that of `straight`, which has no handler; `caught` adds none. Whoever lets the mark through a handler has to put the counts back there too. f3 = straight, f4 = caught
